# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  CLIENT (frontend) environment variables
#  Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values.
#  Vite exposes any var prefixed with VITE_ to the client via
#  import.meta.env.VITE_*. API calls use relative /api paths resolved
#  by the Vite dev proxy (see vite.config.js) in development, and by
#  the Express static/SPA server in production. Firebase config is
#  read from VITE_FIREBASE_* below (src/firebase/firebaseConfig.js);
#  a built-in fallback is used when these are unset, so the app runs
#  out of the box — set your own for production.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Firebase web config — read by src/firebase/firebaseConfig.js.
# Optional in dev (a fallback config is used if unset); set your own
# project's values for production.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_firebase_api_key
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=000000000000
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:xxxxxxxxxxxx

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  InkWell AI — the writing studio's copilot.
#
#  With none of these set, every AI surface on /create-blog shows its
#  honest offline state ("AI is currently unavailable.") and everything
#  else — the editor, autosave, publishing — works normally.
#
#  Two ways to configure (services/aiService.js, in this order):
#
#  1. PROXY (recommended): point VITE_AI_BASE_URL at an endpoint YOU own
#     (an Express route on the server is ideal — it can hold the real
#     provider key server-side and never ship it to the browser). The
#     client POSTs { system, prompt, history } and expects back JSON with
#     the reply in one of: { output } | { text } | { output_text }.
#     Leave VITE_AI_PROVIDER unset when using a proxy.
#
#     VITE_AI_BASE_URL=https://your-server.example.com/api/ai/draft
#     # Optional bearer token the client sends as `Authorization`
#     VITE_AI_API_KEY=
#
#  2. DIRECT PROVIDER: bring-your-own-key from the browser. Fine for
#     local experiments; NOT recommended for production (the key ships
#     in the page bundle to every visitor).
#
#       VITE_AI_PROVIDER=openai     # "openai" | "gemini" | "anthropic"
#       VITE_AI_API_KEY=            # the provider key — never commit it
#       VITE_AI_MODEL=              # e.g. gpt-4o-mini / gemini-2.0-flash /
#                                   # claude-3-5-haiku-20241022 (a sensible
#                                   # default model is used when unset)
#
#  Do NOT put real keys in this file or in any committed .env — keys are
#  read from the environment only.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_AI_PROVIDER=
VITE_AI_API_KEY=
VITE_AI_MODEL=
VITE_AI_BASE_URL=